1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,917
Falah: Calgary has something on every night. The hard part isn’t finding an event.

2
00:00:05,917 --> 00:00:07,583
It’s walking in alone.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,750
Hunter: Nearly one in four young Canadians often feels lonely.

4
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:15,500
More than one in four lives with a disability.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,083
And Calgary is growing faster than it has in forty years.

6
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:26,400
Falah: Tandem is a group-first way to find people to do things with.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:30,983
No follower counts, no feeds, and we rate events, never people.

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:38,200
Hunter: Meet Riley: visiting Calgary for ten days, and anxious in big groups.

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:45,033
Falah: Sign-up is one tap with Google, and choosing “Visiting Calgary” turns on travel mode.

10
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,683
Hunter: Riley picks a few interests.

11
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:53,617
Falah: Comfort needs stay private, and they’re never medical labels: small groups, quiet, beginner-friendly.

12
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:59,517
Hunter: And Ease Into It moves low-pressure events to the top of every list.

13
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:05,400
Falah: Now Riley just types what they want, or says it out loud.

14
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:12,783
Hunter: Our parser turns plain words into real filters, and accessibility filters only count what organizers have confirmed.

15
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:16,433
Falah: And every result explains why it was picked.

16
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:23,867
Hunter: The map runs on the exact same filters, so the list and the map always agree.

17
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:28,450
Tap a pin, and you can join right from the map.

18
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:35,550
Falah: Riley can see exactly how this match was scored: interests, timing, distance, access and budget.

19
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:37,633
It’s rule-based, with no tracking.

20
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:40,783
Hunter: One tap, and Riley’s going.

21
00:01:40,783 --> 00:01:48,700
The page says what to expect, that it’s First-Time Friendly, and which access features the host has actually confirmed.

22
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:56,033
Falah: Joining unlocks the group chat, so Riley can say hi before ever walking in.

23
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:00,133
Hunter: And that reply came from the host’s phone.

24
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:07,217
Our Tandem Live server streams each change to every device in about a tenth of a second.

25
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,750
Falah: If the server goes down, Riley can keep chatting.

26
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:16,750
Messages are saved on the device and delivered once the server’s back.

27
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:25,967
Hunter: Because Riley’s visiting, Explore Like a Local plans the weekend around their interests and comfort settings.

28
00:02:25,967 --> 00:02:28,467
One tap joins the whole plan.

29
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:37,300
Falah: After the book club, Riley confirms they went, and earns Tandem Miles for showing up, not for popularity.

30
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,933
Falah: Then Riley rates the event. Never the people.

31
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:49,217
Hunter: The leaderboard uses a Bayesian average, so a handful of five-star reviews can’t outrank an event that’s consistently great.

32
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,583
Falah: Here’s the bigger picture: accessibility isn’t hidden in a settings page.

33
00:02:54,583 --> 00:03:00,833
Bigger text, a font designed for low vision, and high contrast change every screen instantly.

34
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:03,750
And any page can be read aloud.

35
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:11,633
Hunter: Riley decides who sees what, and can download or delete their data any time.

36
00:03:11,633 --> 00:03:14,967
Passwords, IDs and medical details are never stored.

37
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:22,433
Hunter: Under the hood: React 19 and TypeScript, with every rule a pure, tested function.

38
00:03:22,433 --> 00:03:29,100
Live sync is our own Node server in Docker, and Supabase is ready for city scale.

39
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:36,967
Falah: Every core workflow is tested end to end, with zero automated accessibility violations across 18 pages.

40
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:41,433
Falah: Tandem doesn’t measure how many people follow you.

41
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:45,350
Hunter: It helps you find people to go somewhere with.
